# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form — Formspree + Cloudflare Turnstile
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. This file is committed; .env is not. Copy it to .env and
# fill in the real values from the Formspree and Cloudflare dashboards.
#
# Both variables below are PUBLIC by design and ship in the browser bundle.
# That is correct for this build and is not a leak:
#   - the Formspree endpoint is a public POST target; abuse is what Turnstile
#     and the honeypot are for
#   - a Turnstile SITEKEY is public by specification
#
# The Turnstile SECRET key is NOT a variable in this project and must never
# enter this repo — not here, not in .env, not in a comment, not in a commit
# message. Formspree stores it in its own dashboard and verifies the token
# server-side. There is no server in this project to hold it; the site is
# fully static.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Formspree form endpoint. Dashboard -> your form -> Integration -> AJAX.
# Format: https://formspree.io/f/<form_id>
PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/your_form_id

# Cloudflare Turnstile sitekey, from the widget's dashboard entry.
# Format: 0x<alphanumeric>
#
# MANAGED mode. The mode is load-bearing — the build is measured against a
# visible ~300px widget, and invisible mode renders nothing and would orphan
# every narrow-viewport measurement. The widget's hostname list must carry
# drsyreetamcclain.com, www.drsyreetamcclain.com and localhost.
#
# NEVER pair a live sitekey with a TEST secret, or the reverse. A test sitekey
# emits a dummy token that only a test secret validates; the mismatch fails
# every submission and reads as a broken build rather than a config error.
# Cloudflare's test sitekeys, for local work with a matching test secret:
#   1x00000000000000000000AA  always passes
#   2x00000000000000000000AB  always fails
#   3x00000000000000000000FF  forces the interactive challenge
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=your_turnstile_sitekey
